   "blocking": true,
   "fix": null,
   "harm": "returning a raw CNode pointer after unlocking m_nodes_mutex risks leaving callers with a dangling pointer if another thread deletes the node",
   "hash": "0f1c0d952a8b1a20",
   "history": [
    {
     "at": "2026-09-18T03:33:46+00:00",
     "blocking": true,
     "by": "run:20260918-0314",
     "cause": "rc:1935423919",
     "status": "open"
    }
   ],
   "id": "rc:1935423919",
   "kind": "safety",
   "pin": null,
   "quote": "An issue here is that we return a CNode*, unlock m_nodes_mutex, then another thread comes along and deletes the node - leaving the caller with a dangling pointer.",
   "settled_by": null,
   "status": "open",
   "url": "https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/30988#discussion_r1935423919"
  },
  {
   "association": "MEMBER",
   "at": "2025-03-05",
   "author": "theuni",
   "author_replies": [
    "c:2703769420",
    "c:2792622898"
   ],
   "blocking": true,
   "fix": null,
   "harm": "SockMan mimics a generic I/O framework without its features, remains tightly coupled to Core's P2P send/recv model, and is ill-suited for HTTP or SV2",
   "hash": "3ad08a8f1d1648b6",
   "history": [
    {
     "at": "2026-09-18T03:33:46+00:00",
     "blocking": true,
     "by": "run:20260918-0314",
     "cause": "c:2702063374",
     "status": "open"
    }
   ],
   "id": "c:2702063374",
   "kind": "approach",
   "pin": null,
   "quote": "I believe this is the wrong abstraction level. SockMan is essentially mimicking the behavior of a generic io multiplexing framework (libevent, libuv, etc.), but without the feature-set of those libs.",
   "settled_by": null,
   "status": "open",
   "url": "https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/30988#issuecomment-2702063374"
  },
  {
   "association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
   "at": "2025-11-17",
   "author": "ryanofsky",
   "author_replies": [
    "c:4004005383"
   ],
   "blocking": false,
   "fix": null,
   "harm": "maintaining separate unordered maps to link connection IDs, sockets, and metadata is fragile and prone to getting out of sync",
   "hash": "e091a8aaa0926e88",
   "history": [
    {
     "at": "2026-09-18T03:33:46+00:00",
     "blocking": false,
     "by": "run:20260918-0314",
     "cause": "rc:2534287896",
     "status": "open"
    }
   ],
   "id": "rc:2534287896",
   "kind": "interface",
   "pin": null,
   "quote": "It would seem less fragile to just replace the m_permissions field with a more generic field like std::any m_metadata or std::any m_user_data instead of requiring the application to maintain a separate unordered map and needing to deal with conditions when the map and vector could get out of sync",
   "settled_by": null,
   "status": "open",
   "url": "https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/30988#discussion_r2534287896"
  }
 ],
